@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
# Para API corriendo en Docker Compose, cambiar a: http://localhost:5080

### 1. Health Checks
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready
Accept: application/json

### 2. Login Administrador (PBAC completo)
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@enterprise.local",
  "password": "Admin123*"
}

### 2b. Login Usuario Estándar (Solo lectura en Categorías, Productos y Movimientos)
# @name loginUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@enterprise.local",
  "password": "User123*"
}

### 3. Consultar Sesión Actual y Permisos (/auth/me)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4. Rotar Refresh Token (RTR)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{loginAdmin.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

### 5. Listar Usuarios (Requiere Users.Read)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 6. Crear Categoría (Categorías CRUD)
# @name createCategory
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "ELEC",
  "name": "Electrónica y Cómputo",
  "description": "Equipos portátiles, periféricos y accesorios de oficina"
}

### 7. Listar Categorías Paginadas
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories?page=1&pageSize=10&isActive=true
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8. Obtener Categoría por ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 9. Actualizar Categoría
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "ELEC",
  "name": "Electrónica Corporativa",
  "description": "Equipamiento tecnológico empresarial",
  "isActive": true
}

### 10. Crear Producto (Productos CRUD)
# @name createProduct
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "LAP-PRO-14",
  "name": "Laptop Workstation 14 Pro",
  "description": "Portátil 16GB RAM, SSD 512GB NVMe",
  "categoryId": "{{createCategory.response.body.id}}",
  "price": 1450.00,
  "initialStock": 10,
  "minStock": 4
}

### 11. Listar Productos con Filtros (paginado, categoría, stock bajo, búsqueda)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products?page=1&pageSize=10&categoryId={{createCategory.response.body.id}}&lowStockOnly=false&search=LAP
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 11b. Consultar Productos por Categoría (US-004 — valida existencia de categoría)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.id}}/products?page=1&pageSize=10&isActive=true&lowStockOnly=false
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 12. Obtener Producto por ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{createProduct.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 13. Actualizar Producto (El stock NO se sobrescribe aquí; se gestiona vía Kardex)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{createProduct.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "LAP-PRO-14",
  "name": "Laptop Workstation 14 Pro Gen2",
  "description": "Portátil 32GB RAM, SSD 1TB NVMe",
  "categoryId": "{{createCategory.response.body.id}}",
  "price": 1590.00,
  "minStock": 5,
  "isActive": true
}

### 14. Registrar Movimiento de Inventario: ENTRADA (ENTRY)
# @name createEntryMovement
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/inventory-movements
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{createProduct.response.body.id}}",
  "type": "ENTRY",
  "quantity": 15,
  "reason": "Ingreso por orden de compra OC-2026-0041"
}

### 15. Registrar Movimiento de Inventario: SALIDA (EXIT)
# @name createExitMovement
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/inventory-movements
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{createProduct.response.body.id}}",
  "type": "EXIT",
  "quantity": 4,
  "reason": "Despacho a cliente factura FV-9821"
}

### 16. Consultar Historial Kardex de Movimientos con Filtros
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/inventory-movements?page=1&pageSize=10&productId={{createProduct.response.body.id}}&type=EXIT
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 17. Consultar Detalle de Movimiento por ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/inventory-movements/{{createExitMovement.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 18. Eliminar Producto (Regla: solo sin stock > 0 ni movimientos en Kardex; si ya tiene, devuelve 409 Conflict)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{createProduct.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 19. Eliminar Categoría (Regla: bloqueado con 409 Conflict si tiene productos asociados)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 20. Cerrar Sesión e Invalidar JWT (Blacklist O(1) + Revocación de Refresh Tokens)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}
